{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "The current best is config_026 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.7250 accuracy. All four aggregation/fusion combinations with scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l have been tested, confirming transformer+weighted as optimal. The key remaining uncertainty is the image encoder's contribution when paired with the dominant scvi_n200 RNA encoder: in scgpt experiments, imagenet_vit_l beat resnet50 by ~1.7%, but with the much stronger scvi_n200 encoder the gap may narrow. Config_010 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) tests this directly. If it approaches 0.725, it offers a significantly cheaper alternative (resnet50 is ~half the cost of imagenet_vit_l, estimated ~2.0–2.5 GPU hours vs ~3.6). If it underperforms, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is essential and locks in config_026 as the final answer. As the last experiment, this is the highest-information test among remaining options: it either finds a cheaper near-equivalent or definitively validates the current best. No other untested configuration (pca_n2000, singleprofile, rna_only) has a plausible path to exceeding 0.725 given the strong evidence for scvi_n200 + multimodal + multiprofile."
}

